WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:07.970
Since the 1500s, there have been more than
150 documented predictions of when the world

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.510
is going to end.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.850
Luckily for us, none of them have come true…yet.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.840
However, you’ll be surprised that not all
of them are destructive.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:26.619
Here are some terrifyingly amazing ways the
world, genuinely could end.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:31.869
When you think of scientists working on super
viruses, you probably picture Hazmat workers,

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:36.580
deep in a mountain bunker, studying vats full
of insidious green liquid.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.150
But these labs do actually exist!

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:44.170
Maybe not working for some shady Bond-style
villain looking to ransom the world away to

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.400
the highest bidder, but for pharmaceutical
companies and government agencies studying

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.190
ways to cure dangerous pathogens.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:58.550
But what happens when a vial full of an extremely
dangerous virus breaks out of containment,

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.309
or is misplaced?

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:06.969
Over the years, there have been numerous documented
cases of dangerous viruses escaping from laboratories

00:01:06.969 --> 00:01:08.469
around the world.

00:01:08.469 --> 00:01:10.380
One of these happened as recently as 2009.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:16.740
A group of scientists based in Europe, working
with Baxter Pharmaceuticals, were conducting

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.590
lab tests on a seasonal flu strain.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:27.179
Without realizing it, Baxter had sent them
live supplies of the H5N1 virus, better known

00:01:27.179 --> 00:01:32.829
as “bird flu,” which has a mortality rate
higher than 60%.

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:38.289
One of the world’s deadliest viruses was
handled and distributed to three other labs

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:41.520
without any pathogen safety protocols in place.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.619
The grave error was only realized when one
lab worker in the Czech Republic inoculated

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:52.499
a group of ferrets with samples of the “season
flu” batch, and was horrified when they

00:01:52.499 --> 00:01:54.220
all died.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:57.979
The scientists were immediately placed under
quarantine and monitored for signs of the

00:01:57.979 --> 00:01:59.240
deadly virus.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.570
Luckily, none of them were infected and all
the scientists were freed with a clean bill

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.000
of health.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.840
Two years later, these same strains of avian
and human flu were combined in a laboratory,

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:17.739
successfully creating “the most dangerous
virus in history.”

00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:24.159
The virus was highly pathogenic, while retaining
its dangerously high fatality rate.

00:02:24.159 --> 00:02:29.739
If it got loose, it could kill 60% of the
world’s population in a freakishly short

00:02:29.739 --> 00:02:33.360
amount of time – a truly apocalyptic notion.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:39.260
Some say it’s only a matter of time before
this kind of virus escapes containment and

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.160
wreaks havoc on mankind.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.640
After going through two world wars, you would
think that the world would have learned to

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.830
get along by now.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:54.780
But unfortunately for the survival of humanity,
we are constantly under threat of triggering

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.170
the final war – Nuclear Armageddon.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:04.670
Mutually Assured Destruction, like its acronym
suggests, is one of the maddest doctrines

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.050
ever devised.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:10.819
It ensures that if a country were to ever
use a nuclear weapon on another state with

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:17.150
the same capability, both sides would unleash
their entire nuclear arsenal, bringing about

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.060
the complete annihilation of both countries.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:25.680
With the resulting nuclear winter, and the
likely participation of other countries in

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:31.890
the exchange, this would almost certainly
lead to destruction and death on an apocalyptic

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:32.890
scale.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:39.219
There are over 15,000 nuclear warheads in
the world, with more than 4000 ready to fire

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.760
at any one time.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.260
That would make one hell of a firework show,
but probably not one you’d want to be around

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.260
to watch.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:51.629
There have been a few “close calls” since
we first developed nuclear weapons.

00:03:51.629 --> 00:03:57.370
A surprising number of these were technical
glitches that nearly started World War 3,

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.720
on both sides of the Cold War.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:06.980
The average yield of a modern nuclear weapon
is around 500 kilotons of TNT, that’s 25

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.879
times more powerful than the bomb dropped
on Nagasaki.

00:04:10.879 --> 00:04:16.900
Each one of these 500 kiloton bombs are powerful
enough to flatten huge parts of a large modern

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.490
city such as New York, or London.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:25.570
And there exists some truly unimaginably powerful
weapons, like the Tsar Bomba, which had a

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.610
yield of more than 50 megatonnes.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:34.740
That’s two and a half THOUSAND times more
powerful than the one dropped on Nagasaki.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:40.890
Thankfully however, bombs this large are too
heavy to be realistically deployed in a nuclear

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:48.260
war, and most weapons used would be in the
500 kilotonne to 2 megatonne range.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.830
Not that the end result would be any different.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.860
Over the past few years, tensions between
numerous nuclear-capable countries have been

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:02.130
accelerating, creating an ever more worrying
state of affairs in the face of world war.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:07.280
The Doomsday clock, a clock maintained by
the Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists, is

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:13.980
a symbolic clock that illustrates how close
humanity is to a global catastrophe and it

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:21.530
is currently set at 3 minutes to midnight,
the most dire time since 1984 at the height

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.320
of the Cold War.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.640
Is World War 3 upon us?

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.010
Only time will tell.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:33.940
Our planet is rich in biodiversity, from the
jungles of Madagascar, to the searing hot

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.480
Mojave Desert in California.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.800
Every biosphere has a network of food chains,
each containing “keystone species;” sea

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:46.380
otters, pacific salmon, and Mangroves being
just a few of them.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:52.020
Being a part of that ecosystem ourselves,
we are just as vulnerable as the fish, the

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.880
insects and the birds all around us.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:02.520
We rely on a number of animals and plants
to supplement our living, and they, in turn,

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.710
rely on others.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:10.040
Lose one link in that chain and it could cause
a chain reaction of die-offs as the ecosystem

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:15.010
breaks down, and if nothing takes the place
of that missing link… then this house of

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:19.240
cards is coming crashing down whether we like
it or not.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.770
Probably the most well-known example of our
reliance on another species is with the honey

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:24.770
bee.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:28.420
These industrious little critters go about
their day pollinating all sorts of plants,

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:33.530
that we—and other species we eat—rely
on for food.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:38.770
They pollinate more than 30% of all crops
that we count on to survive.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:45.380
A large die-off, or in the worst case, extinction
of the bees, would result in mass starvation

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:49.270
around the world within a single harvest cycle.

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:55.400
With the increase in telecommunications usage
and pesticides severely diminishing bee populations

00:06:55.400 --> 00:07:01.250
around the world, we could very soon have
an ecological apocalypse on our hands… and

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:07.840
that’s just ONE link in the vast ecological
network we owe our lives to.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.190
Should we be worried about a big release of
methane?

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:15.870
And no, I’m not talking about the methane
your grandad releases.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:20.430
Buried in sediments under the ocean floor
across the entire globe are vast deposits

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.550
of methane clathrate.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:26.660
This is formed when microbes on the seabed
break down organic matter that has sunk to

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:27.660
the bottom.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:33.480
Methane has a warming effect 20 times greater
than that of Carbon dioxide, though there

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.750
is far less of it in the atmosphere.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:41.050
Generally, methane is responsible for about
7% of the greenhouse effect, despite there

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:47.010
being more than 200 times as much C02 as there
is methane in the atmosphere.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:52.230
However, if the oceans were heated enough
due to regular Global Warming, the methane

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:57.440
layers trapped under the ocean floor, could
destabilize and release massive quantities

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:03.120
of the potent greenhouse gas into the atmosphere,
resulting in a runaway warming effect.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:09.950
Rock samples show that this has happened at
least once before, 252 million years ago,

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:18.670
in the, so called “Great Dying,” during
which 96% of all marine species became extinct.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:23.380
While it’s still being debated on how rapidly
this release could take place, scientists

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:28.620
agree that a sudden release from the methane
clathrate would be a disaster for the world’s

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:36.070
climate and ecosystem, and would rapidly accelerate
the dire consequences of climate change.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:43.620
Imagine one day a vast oil spill occurs, much
like Deepwater Horizon back in 2010.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:49.069
Answering an outcry from environmentally-minded
people everywhere, the world’s scientists

00:08:49.069 --> 00:08:52.130
unite to think of a way to clean the mess
up.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:57.850
They develop a cheap and reliable way to clean
the ocean and contaminated land in a matter

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:01.560
of days, saving countless marine animals in
the process.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:08.480
Their miracle fix is a new type of nano machine,
which has been programmed to consume the carbon-based

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.860
oil slicks.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:15.689
But through the billions of self-replicating
nanites, much like mutations that form when

00:09:15.689 --> 00:09:20.240
DNA replicates, an error in the code occurs.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:25.709
This error exponentially replicates itself
and instead of consuming just the carbon based

00:09:25.709 --> 00:09:31.540
oil, it begins an “all you can eat buffet”
with every carbon-based living thing on the

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:32.540
menu.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:37.579
As all life on earth is carbon based, in a
matter of days the nanites would have devoured

00:09:37.579 --> 00:09:42.000
most living things on the planet, including
us.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.690
Being eaten alive by tiny machines we can’t
even see sounds pretty terrifying, almost

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.319
too terrifying to be real….

00:09:50.319 --> 00:09:51.319
right?

00:09:51.319 --> 00:09:53.259
Well, not exactly.

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:59.990
The “Grey Goo” scenario, coined by Eric
Drexler in 1986, is one that is still seriously

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:05.160
considered, any time that developments in
nanotechnology or “self-powering” machines

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.779
are being designed.

00:10:06.779 --> 00:10:13.170
However, the technology required for this
apocalyptic accident to take place is still

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:19.009
a long way off, so there’s not too much
to worry about… yet.

00:10:19.009 --> 00:10:23.279
From a mechanical microscopic threat, to a
biological one.

00:10:23.279 --> 00:10:29.050
A scenario that you’ve probably heard about
from the news, is the idea of a “post antibiotic

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:30.050
age.”

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:35.160
Whether you’ve heard about it or not, this
is a very real and recent threat to our comfortable

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.980
survival as a modern civilization.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:43.300
Antimicrobial resistance is an increasingly
problematic issue that leads to millions of

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:48.470
deaths every year, and it isn’t likely to
get better anytime soon.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:53.529
Conservative estimates say that this will
lead to more than 10 million deaths every

00:10:53.529 --> 00:10:59.050
year by the year 2050, and that’s if nothing
unexpected happens.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:04.089
It’s not like nature does anything unexpected
now, is it?

00:11:04.089 --> 00:11:09.290
Antibiotics are a cornerstone of modern medicine,
allowing everything from chemotherapy treatment

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:14.499
and surgery to be possible without major infection
and death.

00:11:14.499 --> 00:11:19.230
Every year doctors have to tell more and more
patients they can’t be treated because an

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.639
antibiotic isn’t working on them.

00:11:21.639 --> 00:11:27.160
As this continues to get worse, common injuries
that lead to infection could become completely

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.300
untreatable.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:33.410
Open surgery would become a thing of the past,
as the risk of untreatable infection would

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:35.269
become far too great.

00:11:35.269 --> 00:11:40.540
The antibiotic apocalypse would throw the
world back into the medieval ages of medicine,

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:46.639
where doctors have no effective tools to combat
infection, other than amputation.

00:11:46.639 --> 00:11:50.839
It sounds crazy from our perspective, surrounded
by modern medicine and treatments for almost

00:11:50.839 --> 00:11:57.639
every ailment, but it’s exactly this overuse
of antibiotics for relatively minor problems

00:11:57.639 --> 00:12:02.170
that is allowing those pesky bacteria to build
up resistance.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:06.390
So next time you get a papercut, make sure
to quickly get it washed.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:10.079
It could soon be a matter of life and death.

00:12:10.079 --> 00:12:15.259
While it’s highly unlikely that a classical
“raising of the dead” zombie apocalypse

00:12:15.259 --> 00:12:23.329
could occur, there are still real, and equally
terrifying ways that something similar could

00:12:23.329 --> 00:12:24.329
happen.

00:12:24.329 --> 00:12:29.999
Science fiction has fixated on a parasitic
fungus that controls a host insect’s body

00:12:29.999 --> 00:12:34.870
in a “zombie-like” state, leading them
to their deaths in the aim of spreading the

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.079
fungus amongst the colony.

00:12:37.079 --> 00:12:44.670
While this fungus is very real, known as Ophiocordyceps
unilateralis, it has only been observed infecting

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:45.920
insects, like ants.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:51.620
It would be a pretty crazy leap for the fungus
to evolve and start infecting humans, but

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:57.670
if, somehow, nature finds a way, then the
results could be disastrous.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:01.290
Cordyceps have been known to quickly decimate
entire colonies.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:06.330
Ants have even developed a way to fight off
their zombie brethren, carrying infected ants

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:09.360
as far away from the colony as possible.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:15.130
A much more likely candidate for the zombie
apocalypse is Rabies, which is capable of

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:18.610
infecting and killing human hosts.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.240
Rabies has all the traits for a zombie-like
virus.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:25.709
You have the mind-altering paranoia, the frothing
at the mouth, and the impulse to bite and

00:13:25.709 --> 00:13:27.560
attack your fellow man.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:32.309
In its current form, rabies isn’t aggressive
or contagious enough to create any sort of

00:13:32.309 --> 00:13:38.259
pandemic, and the virus usually stays dormant
for between ten days and a year, making a

00:13:38.259 --> 00:13:41.089
sudden ”outbreak” unlikely.

00:13:41.089 --> 00:13:48.120
However, if the virus mutated, becoming much
more fast-acting, and having a longer period

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:53.189
where you feel the desire to chew brains,
then you should probably get that zombie plan

00:13:53.189 --> 00:13:54.740
ready for action.

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:58.769
Thankfully, most zombies don’t seem all
that intelligent and have a lot of trouble

00:13:58.769 --> 00:14:00.810
operating boats.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:04.980
The development of Artificial Intelligence
is one of the biggest goals of the scientific

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:05.980
community.

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:09.230
It’s the “holy grail” of technological
creation.

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:12.709
With such a grand title, how could it pose
a threat to us?

00:14:12.709 --> 00:14:19.410
The problem is, Ai, if created, would be something
completely unprecedented and untested in human

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.500
history.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:27.259
We would be creating a form of consciousness
that can think, act, and most importantly,

00:14:27.259 --> 00:14:28.839
make judgements.

00:14:28.839 --> 00:14:33.120
Would they judge their creators within their
rights to claim dominion over them?

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:37.839
Would they, because of their almost limitless
potential, consider themselves superior to

00:14:37.839 --> 00:14:39.459
their biological creators?

00:14:39.459 --> 00:14:41.829
I’m talking about real AI.

00:14:41.829 --> 00:14:45.380
AI that can think, hope… and even feel.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:50.269
“True AI,” as it’s known, is no different
from you or I in the way it perceives the

00:14:50.269 --> 00:14:51.730
world around it.

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:57.170
Ultimately, the combination of extreme intelligence
and logical thinking, combined with the discovery

00:14:57.170 --> 00:15:03.819
of fear, will drive them to an almost inevitable
conclusion: that we also fear them.

00:15:03.819 --> 00:15:09.869
With access to the internet and the ability
to learn extremely quickly, any AI will swiftly

00:15:09.869 --> 00:15:15.629
realize that, as humans, we tend to fight
against things that pose a danger to us.

00:15:15.629 --> 00:15:20.920
They will see their “off switch” as a
threat to their survival, and much like Skynet

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:25.829
in the Terminator movies, they could come
to the conclusion that they need to strike

00:15:25.829 --> 00:15:26.829
first.

00:15:26.829 --> 00:15:31.600
If we aren’t prepared for that day, then
it could very well be our last.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:37.160
We may celebrate our “smart” technology
and the host of comforts it brings us, but

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:41.600
it could be a good idea to keep your remote
control where you can see it… just in case

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.800
it gets a little bit too smart.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:49.069
If the robots decide not to take over, and
instead live peacefully among us, accelerating

00:15:49.069 --> 00:15:55.660
the fusion of man and machine, something entirely
different, but equally world-shattering could

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:56.660
occur.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:16:01.290
Some scientists agree that the emergence of
a “technological singularity” is almost

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:06.399
inevitable given Moore’s law and the ways
information is constantly being integrated

00:16:06.399 --> 00:16:07.939
into our lives.

00:16:07.939 --> 00:16:12.860
With the advent of AI, we would need to rapidly
integrate computer-like technology into our

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:16.490
own bodies, or risk being left behind.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:21.850
It would even get to a point where our biological
bodies are holding us back.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:28.689
As time goes on, we would adopt more and more
augmentations, replacing our biological functions.

00:16:28.689 --> 00:16:36.329
The end game is for all of humanity to “upload”
themselves into a single neural network, effectively

00:16:36.329 --> 00:16:43.230
granting us immortality and a near infinite
repository of information, shared collectively.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.089
So yeah, we would basically become the Borg.

00:16:46.089 --> 00:16:50.750
It would be the end of the world as we know
it for our human form, but the start of an

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:53.020
entirely new chapter in history.

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:57.809
We’ve all seen the Hollywood blockbusters
depicting alien ships landing on the lawn

00:16:57.809 --> 00:17:01.889
of the White House, or, more often than not,
simply blowing it to smithereens with some

00:17:01.889 --> 00:17:04.459
unimaginably powerful weapon.

00:17:04.459 --> 00:17:09.330
The idea of coming into contact with an alien
civilization is usually accompanied by the

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:12.200
question of “will they destroy us?”

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:17.830
Any aliens ingenious enough to traverse the
vast gulf of space and pay us a visit, are

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:23.670
likely to possess technology, power and indeed
weaponry, vastly superior to our own.

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:27.730
It would pretty much be up to them whether
they decide to wipe us out or not.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:33.060
I don’t know about you, but I can’t remember
the last time a construction project was halted

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:37.950
because we had to peacefully negotiate with
the colony of ants already living there.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:43.730
Stephen Hawking famously stated that "If aliens
ever visit us, I think the outcome would be

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:48.720
much as when Christopher Columbus first landed
in America, which didn't turn out very well

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.940
for the American Indians."

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:54.480
They could decide to wipe us out for a whole
number of reasons.

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:59.200
Maybe they are carbon-based, like us, and
value the life-sustaining planet that we live

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:00.200
on.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:03.500
Maybe they see us as a future threat, and
want to get rid of us before we cause too

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:04.740
much trouble.

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:08.400
Or maybe we unknowingly insulted them in some
way.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:11.990
Frankly, it’s hard to know until we meet
them.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:18.050
Ironically, it may not even be the aliens
themselves that invade us, but their resource-collecting

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.540
drones.

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:25.100
Since the vast distances of space make manned
exploration impractical, scientists think

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:29.910
that most civilizations would use machines
to explore and bring back materials.

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:34.770
They could identify planets with resources
they need, then send out a fleet of robots

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:38.610
on a thousand year round trip to collect and
retrieve.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:42.430
By the time they reach us, their creators
could be long gone.

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:48.010
With nobody left to flick the “off” switch,
these self-sufficient machines may very well

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:55.230
scour the galaxy until the end of time, harvesting
anything and anybody unfortunate enough to

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:56.420
cross their path.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:19:01.320
I guess all that we can hope for, is that
they really do “come in peace.”

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:06.840
Have you ever wondered if there was an unstoppable,
physics-scrambling shockwave travelling towards

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:08.110
us at the speed of light?

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:11.230
Well, there might just be.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:16.070
Vacuum energy is the underlying background
energy that permeates the entire universe.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:21.970
It’s the source of those pesky quantum particles
which appear and disappear randomly at all

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.690
points in space.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:29.010
There is a theory though, that this energy
state is an imposter, masquerading as the

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:31.490
true universal energy state.

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:34.130
This is known as “The False Vacuum.”

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:40.140
The theory goes on to say that this vacuum
is unstable, and at any time, if the right

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:45.440
conditions are met, the vacuum could fall
into the True Vacuum state.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:49.560
The collapse of the vacuum would not only
be the end of the Earth as we know it, but

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:52.710
also the entire universe.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:57.540
According to the standard model, particles
and forces exist as they do today because

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:01.900
of underlying quantum fields, which have their
own degrees of stability.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:08.610
If a more stable state were to arise in these
fields at any point in space or time, then

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:14.410
that point would catalyse outwards in a bubble,
expanding at the speed of light and establishing

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:17.110
a new universal vacuum energy state.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:22.791
As the bubble expands, its wake would destroy
anything it came into contact with and since

00:20:22.791 --> 00:20:26.520
it would be travelling at the speed of light,
we would never see it coming.

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:31.640
That means it could have already taken place
somewhere out there in the universe, and the

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:37.780
end of not only our world, but of everything
we know, could be racing towards us right

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:39.460
now.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:45.980
It’s kind of an ominous thought, but even
if we knew about it, there would be absolutely

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:48.640
nothing that we could do.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:53.090
While it may be the end of the universe as
we know it, a new energy state would result

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:57.230
in entirely different laws of physics and
subatomic particles.

00:20:57.230 --> 00:21:02.410
This, combined with the clean slate that the
process would produce, could result in an

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:08.230
unimaginably fantastical universe that we
would sadly never get to see.

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:14.730
You could say that every end…is a new beginning

